ups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441905865000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1V0KcYO9u3mZBXc2YHh1mh\"><img style=\"border:0;vertical-align:middle\" src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/4SGWHe9midrWMDxDIJMQraTMMgnAU71soPZ0D28IOSZcs66TdyRoCqyIhaTt-kwo0YKv2lRo05RkwsGFZdnFhdvy60XdxNlL2U-B=s0-d-e1-ft#http://www.google.com/images/icons/product/groups-32.png\"></a>\r\n          </td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n      </tbody>\r\n    </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"padding:20px;background-color:#f5f5f5\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:arial;color:#222222;padding:0px\">\r\n  <a name=\"m_3888353588250359564_m_6398759773049268274_digest_top\" style=\"font-size:21px\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n  \r\n    Today&#39;s topic summary\r\n  \r\n  \r\n  </a><br>\r\n  <span style=\"font-size:11px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/r-inla-discussion-group/topics\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/r-inla-discussion-group/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441905865000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0CabFU2v0c8KE0IlDQFF2f\">View all topics</a>\r\n  </span>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font:13px/18px arial;color:#222222;padding:0px;margin-bottom:30px\">\r\n  <ul style=\"margin-left:3px;padding-left:0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_3888353588250359564_m_6398759773049268274_group_thread_0\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      How can one get the name of a random slope covariate from an inla object?</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">2 Updates</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_3888353588250359564_m_6398759773049268274_group_thread_1\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      Precision to Variance - generic0 model</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_3888353588250359564_m_6398759773049268274_group_thread_2\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">\r\n      R code to run the INLA algorithm</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_3888353588250359564_m_6398759773049268274_group_thread_0\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/t/2813095114ee2a1e?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/t/2813095114ee2a1e?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441905865000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3HoZl2utzP6kXyo25MU8QS\">\r\n      How can one get the name of a random slope covariate from an inla object?\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n    <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n        Helpdesk &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>he...@r-inla.org</a>&gt;: Jun 07 01:05PM +0200\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      not really, as they are constants. you can look at some of them in the<br>\r\nlogfile, like<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n&gt; r = inla(y ~ -1 + f(idx, a, model=&quot;iid&quot;),data = data.frame(y = 1:10,<br>\r\nidx = 1:10, a = 10:1))<br>\r\n&gt; r$logfile\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/msg/6d38166e9b3a6?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/msg/6d38166e9b3a6?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441905865000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1SJWQm394yYsxMlyYK5efB\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n    <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n        Guido Biele &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>guido...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Jun 07 06:46AM -0700\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      thanks,<br>\r\n <br>\r\nI think I also found a way to do it via the formula object:<br>\r\n <br>\r\nassuming &quot;f&quot; is the formula object:<br>\r\n <br>\r\nre = grep(&quot;.f\\\\(&quot;,<br>\r\n          strsplit(as.character(f)[[3]],&quot;\\\\+&quot;)[[1]],\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/msg/b2f0e1138a88f?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/msg/b2f0e1138a88f?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441905865000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1P8FqKo8Wu8FpN4ZeHvZXI\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_3888353588250359564_m_6398759773049268274_digest_top\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_3888353588250359564_m_6398759773049268274_group_thread_1\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/t/fbd98125e3ae0b02?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/t/fbd98125e3ae0b02?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441905865000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3s-moAHh8-u_0NM-gmGbrI\">\r\n      Precision to Variance - generic0 model\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n    <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n        Helpdesk &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>he...@r-inla.org</a>&gt;: Jun 07 01:22PM +0200\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      hopefully, the example below would clarify things. <br>\r\n <br>\r\n&gt; r = inla(y ~ 1, data = data.frame(y = 1:10))<br>\r\n&gt; names(r$marginals.hyperpar)<br>\r\n[1] &quot;Precision for the Gaussian observations&quot;<br>\r\n&gt; mm.var =\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/msg/6d473bb5437dd?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/msg/6d473bb5437dd?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441905865000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1d8-kRmGgcLupZAOZuY9Ul\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_3888353588250359564_m_6398759773049268274_digest_top\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_3888353588250359564_m_6398759773049268274_group_thread_2\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/t/d5b9921d53ae43fc?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/t/d5b9921d53ae43fc?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441905865000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3EOp2MB_wVyhlAOAXFV0wR\">\r\n      R code to run the INLA algorithm\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n    <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n        Helpdesk &lt;<a href rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" data-email-masked>he...@r-inla.org</a>&gt;: Jun 07 01:14PM +0200\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      On Thu, 2019-06-06 at 07:54 -0700, Lars Rönnegård wrote:<br>\r\n&gt; in R for the algorithm, including the numerical integration and<br>\r\n&gt; Laplace approximations. Does anyone have R code to run the INLA\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"